class:: TableMorph2D
summary:: Bilinear traversal of a mipmapped two-dimensional wavetable grid
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

TableMorph2D treats a wavetable bank as a rectangular surface. code::x:: and
code::y:: move continuously across four neighboring tables while code::freq::
reads the interpolated waveform. Prepared mip levels reduce high-frequency
aliasing.

The mono buffer layout is exactly
code::[mip][y][x][sample]::. Every table has code::tableSize:: samples and the
total buffer length must equal
code::mipLevels * tablesY * tablesX * tableSize::. The UGen validates that
declaration once, remembers the buffer identity, and becomes silent with one
server error if the buffer is freed or replaced.

Internally, the UGen performs periodic sample interpolation, bilinear spatial
interpolation, and a frequency-dependent crossfade between adjacent mip
levels. The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/VOsc::. Both scan wavetable
data, but TableMorph2D interpolates a declared two-dimensional grid and manages
mip selection explicitly.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: bufnum
Number of a mono buffer prepared in the documented layout.

argument:: freq
Signed playback frequency in hertz. Negative values read backward.

argument:: x
Horizontal grid position from code::0:: through code::1::. Values outside the
range are clamped.

argument:: y
Vertical grid position from code::0:: through code::1::. Values outside the
range are clamped.

argument:: phase
Readout phase offset in radians.

argument:: tablesX
Initialization-rate column count from code::1:: through code::1024::.

argument:: tablesY
Initialization-rate row count from code::1:: through code::1024::.

argument:: tableSize
Initialization-rate power of two from code::64:: through code::65536::.

argument:: mipLevels
Initialization-rate integer from code::1:: through code::16::.

argument:: interpolation
Initialization-rate mode: code::0:: nearest, code::1:: linear, or code::2::
cubic.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
A mono audio-rate signal.

method:: prepareBuffer

argument:: server
The server that will own the buffer. The default is code::Server.default::.

argument:: tables
A row-major collection of code::tablesX * tablesY:: equal-length sample
collections containing finite values. Only procedural or appropriately
licensed tables should be used.

argument:: tablesX
Literal horizontal dimension from code::1:: through code::1024::.

argument:: tablesY
Literal vertical dimension from code::1:: through code::1024::.

argument:: mipLevels
Number of stored mip levels, from code::1:: through code::16::.

argument:: normalize
If true, remove DC and peak-normalize every source table. DC is always removed.

argument:: action
Function passed to link::Classes/Buffer#*loadCollection:: after loading.

returns::
The allocated Buffer. Buffer loading is asynchronous; call code::s.sync::
before starting a Synth when using the return value directly.

method:: kr

TableMorph2D is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

The dimensions are never inferred from the buffer length. Reallocating or
freeing the buffer while a Synth is active makes that instance permanently
silent. Spatial controls may run at audio rate and are interpolated sample by
sample.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var size = 256;
    var tables = [
        Signal.sineFill(size, [1]),
        Signal.sineFill(size, [1, 0.35]),
        Signal.sineFill(size, [0, 1]),
        Signal.sineFill(size, [1, 0, 0.25])
    ];
    var buffer = TableMorph2D.prepareBuffer(s, tables, 2, 2, 4);
    s.sync;
    {
        TableMorph2D.ar(
            buffer, 90, 0.2, 0.8,
            tablesX: 2, tablesY: 2,
            tableSize: size, mipLevels: 4
        ) * 0.08
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var size = 512;
    var tables = 9.collect { |index|
        Signal.sineFill(size, [1, index / 12, index / 24])
    };
    var buffer = TableMorph2D.prepareBuffer(s, tables, 3, 3, 5);
    s.sync;
    {
        TableMorph2D.ar(
            buffer, 70,
            LFTri.kr(0.07).range(0, 1),
            LFTri.kr(0.11).range(0, 1),
            tablesX: 3, tablesY: 3,
            tableSize: size, mipLevels: 5
        ) * 0.07
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

